<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28927" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕtaurus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέταυρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of several
				rivers</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river in Umbria, celebrated for the defeat of
				Hasdrubal, the brother of Hannibal</i>, now <i>Meturo</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 27, 43 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			486</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕtau-rus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of Metaurus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Metaurum flumen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 4, 38</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river in the Bruttian territory</i>, now <i>Marro</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 10, §
		73</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
